    "summary": "A Grade A warehouse in India is a modern, institutionally built facility with roughly 10–12 m clear height, FM2-grade flat flooring rated around 5–7 tonnes/sqm, dock levellers (about one per 10,000 sqft), sprinkler and hydrant fire systems, a 30 m+ truck court, insulated roofing with skylights, and full statutory compliance. Grade B is functional but misses several of these specs; Grade C is basic godown stock. Grade A commands a rent premium of roughly 20–40% over Grade B in the same micro-market, which efficient cube utilisation and lower operating risk often offset.",
